post_install() {
  cat << EOF

╔════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
║                    KIRO-BIN-HARDENED SECURITY NOTICE                       ║
╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

🔒 HARDENED SECURITY FEATURES ENABLED:

  ✓ Strict file permissions (755/644/4755)
  ✓ Chrome-sandbox SUID protection
  ✓ Cryptographic signature verification
  ✓ Enhanced dependency validation

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

🛡️  OPTIONAL SECURITY ENHANCEMENTS:

  1. AppArmor (Mandatory Access Control)
     └─ Profile installed: /usr/share/apparmor/kiro.apparmor
     └─ Enable with:
        sudo pacman -S apparmor
        sudo cp /usr/share/apparmor/kiro.apparmor /etc/apparmor.d/kiro
        sudo apparmor_parser -r /etc/apparmor.d/kiro
        sudo aa-enforce /etc/apparmor.d/kiro

  2. Firejail (Application Sandboxing)
     └─ Install: sudo pacman -S firejail
     └─ Run: firejail kiro

  3. Bubblewrap (Lightweight Sandboxing)
     └─ Install: sudo pacman -S bubblewrap
     └─ Custom sandbox wrapper available

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

📋 SECURITY BEST PRACTICES:

  • Review AppArmor profile before enabling
  • Use sandboxing for untrusted workspaces
  • Keep Kiro updated via: yay -Syu kiro-bin-hardened
  • Monitor logs: journalctl -u apparmor (if enabled)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

📖 Documentation: https://kiro.dev/
🔐 Security: https://aws.amazon.com/security/

EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}

post_remove() {
  cat << EOF

╔════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
║                  KIRO-BIN-HARDENED REMOVAL NOTICE                          ║
╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

🧹 CLEANUP RECOMMENDATIONS:

  • User data preserved in: ~/.config/Kiro, ~/.cache/Kiro
  • AppArmor profile (if installed): /etc/apparmor.d/kiro
  
  To remove user data:
    rm -rf ~/.config/Kiro ~/.cache/Kiro ~/.local/share/Kiro

  To remove AppArmor profile:
    sudo rm /etc/apparmor.d/kiro
    sudo systemctl reload apparmor

EOF
}
